IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-interpretation-time`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (Australia): PART 5, sections 19 to 19E, the machinery-of-government provisions (pass 2).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Pass 1 left these inert as "machinery of government" and as "addressing officials". They are
-- rules about WHOM a reference means and WHEN an act stays valid, and each affects a person who deals with the Commonwealth, so
-- they are encoded: the two decision tables (ss 19, 19A, 19C) as functions from how a provision refers to an authority to a
-- description of who is meant, the saving provisions (ss 19D, 19E) as functions that return "not invalid merely because" or the
-- explicit "not covered" value NOTHING. What the Administrative Arrangements Order says on a given day is NOT in this text: it is
-- outside the sources, so the table results are descriptions ("the Minister administering the Department that deals with the
-- relevant matter on the relevant day"), and the facts a table cell turns on are plain BOOLEAN inputs.
-- Section 19 item 3 reads (a) or (b), and then (c) "in any case": (c) is read as an addition to (a) or (b), not an alternative to
-- them (fork F21). A table result is therefore a LIST.

§ `Part 5: General interpretation rules (machinery of government, ss 19 to 19E)`

§§ `Section 19: references to Ministers`

DECLARE `How a provision refers to a Minister` IS ONE OF
    `by the expression the Minister, without identifying the Minister`
    `by reference to the fact that the Minister administers a law`
    `by title, even if that title no longer exists`
    `by describing a matter for which the Minister is responsible`

DECLARE `Minister identified by the table in section 19` IS ONE OF
    `the Minister, or any of the Ministers, administering the provision on the relevant day, in relation to the relevant matter`
    `the Minister, or any of the Ministers, administering that law on the relevant day, in relation to the relevant matter`
    `the Minister, or any of the Ministers, identified by item 1`
    `the Minister currently identified by the title, or by a substituted reference order under section 19B`
    `any other Minister administering the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the matters for which that Minister is responsible on the relevant day`
    `the Minister, or any of the Ministers, administering the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter on the relevant day`

-- src:425 | (1) If a provision of an Act refers to a Minister, the following table provides which Minister the provision refers to in relation to a particular matter (the relevant matter) on a particular day (the relevant day).
-- src:426 | References to Ministers in Acts
-- src:427 | If the provision …
-- src:428 | then the Minister referred to is …
-- src:429 | 1
-- src:430 | refers to a Minister by using the expression “the Minister”, without identifying the Minister
-- src:431 | the Minister, or any of the Ministers, administering the provision on the relevant day, in relation to the relevant matter.
-- src:432 | 2
-- src:433 | refers to a Minister by reference to the fact that the Minister administers any of the following laws:
-- src:434 | (a) the Act, that provision or another provision of the Act;
-- src:435 | (b) another Act, or a provision of another Act
-- src:436 | the Minister, or any of the Ministers, administering that law on the relevant day, in relation to the relevant matter.
-- src:437 | 3
-- src:438 | refers to a Minister by title (for example, “the Attorney-General” or “the Minister for Industry”), even if that title no longer exists
-- src:439 | (a) if, at the time the provision commenced, or the reference to the Minister was inserted, the Minister referred to by title administered the provision—the Minister, or any of the Ministers, identified by item 1; or
-- src:440 | (b) if paragraph (a) does not apply—the Minister currently identified by the title, or by a substituted reference order under section 19B; or
-- src:441 | (c) in any case—any other Minister administering the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the matters for which the Minister mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) (as the case may be) is responsible on the relevant day.
-- src:442 | 4
-- src:443 | refers to a Minister by describing a matter for which the Minister is responsible (for example, “the Minister responsible for the environment”)
-- src:444 | the Minister, or any of the Ministers, administering the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter on the relevant day.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19(1) (src:425-444)
GIVEN how IS A `How a provision refers to a Minister`
      `at the time the provision commenced, or the reference to the Minister was inserted, the Minister referred to by title administered the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Minister identified by the table in section 19`
`the Ministers a reference means` how `at the time the provision commenced, or the reference to the Minister was inserted, the Minister referred to by title administered the provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `by the expression the Minister, without identifying the Minister` THEN
        LIST `the Minister, or any of the Ministers, administering the provision on the relevant day, in relation to the relevant matter`
    WHEN `by reference to the fact that the Minister administers a law` THEN
        LIST `the Minister, or any of the Ministers, administering that law on the relevant day, in relation to the relevant matter`
    WHEN `by title, even if that title no longer exists` THEN
        IF `at the time the provision commenced, or the reference to the Minister was inserted, the Minister referred to by title administered the provision`
        THEN LIST `the Minister, or any of the Ministers, identified by item 1`,
                  `any other Minister administering the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the matters for which that Minister is responsible on the relevant day`
        ELSE LIST `the Minister currently identified by the title, or by a substituted reference order under section 19B`,
                  `any other Minister administering the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the matters for which that Minister is responsible on the relevant day`
    WHEN `by describing a matter for which the Minister is responsible` THEN
        LIST `the Minister, or any of the Ministers, administering the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter on the relevant day`

DECLARE `Instrument that may be used to work out the reference` IS ONE OF
    `an Administrative Arrangements Order`
    `a substituted reference order under section 19B`
    `any other instrument`

-- src:445 | (2) Instruments including the following, as in force on the relevant day, or any earlier day, may be used to work out which Minister (or Ministers) is referred to under subsection (1):
-- src:446 | (a) an Administrative Arrangements Order;
-- src:447 | (b) a substituted reference order under section 19B.
-- src:448 | Note: Substituted reference orders under section 19B may have effect in relation to days before the orders are made.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19(2) (src:445-448)
GIVEN instrument IS A `Instrument that may be used to work out the reference`
      `it is in force on the relevant day or was in force on an earlier day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`may be used to work out which Minister is referred to` instrument `it is in force on the relevant day or was in force on an earlier day` MEANS
    CONSIDER instrument
    WHEN `any other instrument` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE IF `it is in force on the relevant day or was in force on an earlier day` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:449 | (3) To avoid doubt, if, because of this section, a provision of an Act is taken to require anything to be done by or in relation to any one of 2 or more Ministers, the provision is not taken to require it to be done in any particular case by or in relation to more than one of those Ministers.
-- src:450 | Acting Ministers
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19(3) (src:449-450)
GIVEN `the number of Ministers by or in relation to any one of whom the provision is taken to require a thing to be done` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the most Ministers by or in relation to whom the thing must be done in a particular case` `the number of Ministers by or in relation to any one of whom the provision is taken to require a thing to be done` MEANS
    IF `the number of Ministers by or in relation to any one of whom the provision is taken to require a thing to be done` AT LEAST 2 THEN JUST 1 ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Who may be taken to be the Minister` IS ONE OF
    `the Minister`
    `a Minister for the time being acting for or on behalf of the Minister`
    `a member of the Executive Council for the time being acting for or on behalf of the Minister`
    `anyone else`

-- src:451 | (4) If a provision of an Act refers to a Minister, the reference is taken to include a reference to a Minister or member of the Executive Council for the time being acting for or on behalf of the Minister.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19(4) (src:451)
GIVEN who IS A `Who may be taken to be the Minister`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a reference to a Minister is taken to include` who MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `anyone else` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Section 19A: references to Departments`

DECLARE `How a provision refers to a Department` IS ONE OF
    `by the expression the Department, without identifying the Department`
    `by title, even if that title no longer exists`
    `by describing a matter for which the Department is responsible`

DECLARE `Department identified by the table in section 19A` IS ONE OF
    `the Department of State of the Commonwealth that is administered by the Minister or Ministers administering that provision in relation to the relevant matter, and that deals with that matter`
    `the Department identified by item 1`
    `the Department of State of the Commonwealth identified by the title, or by a substituted reference order under section 19B`
    `any other Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the matters for which that Department is responsible on the relevant day`
    `the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter on the relevant day`

-- src:453 | (1) If a provision of an Act refers to a Department, the following table provides which Department the provision refers to in relation to a particular matter (the relevant matter) on a particular day (the relevant day).
-- src:454 | References to Departments in Acts
-- src:455 | Item
-- src:456 | If the provision …
-- src:457 | then the Department is …
-- src:458 | 1
-- src:459 | refers to a Department by using the expression “the Department”, without identifying the Department
-- src:460 | the Department of State of the Commonwealth that is administered by the Minister or Ministers administering that provision in relation to the relevant matter, and that deals with that matter.
-- src:461 | 2
-- src:462 | refers to a Department by title (for example, “the Attorney-General’s Department” or “the Department of Industry”), even if that title no longer exists
-- src:463 | (a) if, at the time the provision commenced, or the reference to the Department was inserted, the Department referred to by title was administered by the Minister or Ministers administering that provision in relation to the relevant matter—the Department identified by item 1; or
-- src:464 | (b) if paragraph (a) does not apply—the Department of State of the Commonwealth identified by the title, or by a substituted reference order under section 19B; or
-- src:465 | (c) in any case—any other Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the matters for which the Department mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) (as the case may be) is responsible on the relevant day.
-- src:466 | 3
-- src:467 | refers to a Department by describing a matter for which the Department is responsible (for example, “the Department responsible for the environment”)
-- src:468 | the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter on the relevant day.
-- src:469 | Example: A provision of an Act refers to “the Secretary of the Department” but does not identify which Department is referred to. Under item 1, the reference is to the Secretary of the Department administered by the Minister who administers that provision in relation to the relevant matter, and that deals with that matter, as worked out under subsection (2).
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19A(1) (src:453-469)
GIVEN how IS A `How a provision refers to a Department`
      `at the time the provision commenced, or the reference to the Department was inserted, the Department referred to by title was administered by the Minister or Ministers administering that provision in relation to the relevant matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Department identified by the table in section 19A`
`the Departments a reference means` how `at the time the provision commenced, or the reference to the Department was inserted, the Department referred to by title was administered by the Minister or Ministers administering that provision in relation to the relevant matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `by the expression the Department, without identifying the Department` THEN
        LIST `the Department of State of the Commonwealth that is administered by the Minister or Ministers administering that provision in relation to the relevant matter, and that deals with that matter`
    WHEN `by title, even if that title no longer exists` THEN
        IF `at the time the provision commenced, or the reference to the Department was inserted, the Department referred to by title was administered by the Minister or Ministers administering that provision in relation to the relevant matter`
        THEN LIST `the Department identified by item 1`,
                  `any other Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the matters for which that Department is responsible on the relevant day`
        ELSE LIST `the Department of State of the Commonwealth identified by the title, or by a substituted reference order under section 19B`,
                  `any other Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the matters for which that Department is responsible on the relevant day`
    WHEN `by describing a matter for which the Department is responsible` THEN
        LIST `the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter on the relevant day`

-- src:470 | (2) Instruments including the following, as in force on the relevant day, or any earlier day, may be used to work out which Department is identified by the table in subsection (1):
-- src:471 | (a) an Administrative Arrangements Order;
-- src:472 | (b) a substituted reference order under section 19B.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19A(2) (src:470-472)
GIVEN instrument IS A `Instrument that may be used to work out the reference`
      `it is in force on the relevant day or was in force on an earlier day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`may be used to work out which Department is identified` instrument `it is in force on the relevant day or was in force on an earlier day` MEANS
    CONSIDER instrument
    WHEN `any other instrument` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE IF `it is in force on the relevant day or was in force on an earlier day` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 19B: substituted reference orders`

DECLARE `Kind of authority` IS ONE OF
    `a Minister`
    `a Department of State of the Commonwealth`
    `any other Agency within the meaning of the Public Service Act 1999`
    `an office, including an APS employee's office and any other appointment or position, or the holder of an office`
    `something else`

-- The list of authorities is the same in ss 19B(7), 19C(6) and 19D(5); each section's rule cites its own words.
-- src:499 | (7) In this section:
-- src:500 | authority means any of the following:
-- src:501 | (a) a Minister;
-- src:502 | (b) a Department of State of the Commonwealth;
-- src:503 | (c) any other Agency within the meaning of the Public Service Act 1999;
-- src:504 | (d) an office (including an APS employee’s office and any other appointment or position), or the holder of an office.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19B(7) (src:499-504)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of authority`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is an authority within section 19B` kind MEANS
    NOT (kind EQUALS `something else`)

-- src:476 | (1) This section applies if:
-- src:477 | (a) a provision of an Act refers to an authority (see subsection (7)); and
-- src:478 | (b) any of the following happens:
-- src:479 | (i) the authority is abolished;
-- src:480 | (ii) the name or title of the authority is changed;
-- src:481 | (iii) there is a change in the matters dealt with by the authority because of the effect of an Administrative Arrangements Order;
-- src:482 | (iv) the reference to the authority becomes no longer appropriate for any other reason.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19B(1) (src:476-482)
GIVEN `a provision of an Act refers to an authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority is abolished` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name or title of the authority is changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a change in the matters dealt with by the authority because of the effect of an Administrative Arrangements Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference to the authority becomes no longer appropriate for any other reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 19B applies` `a provision of an Act refers to an authority` `the authority is abolished` `the name or title of the authority is changed` `there is a change in the matters dealt with by the authority because of the effect of an Administrative Arrangements Order` `the reference to the authority becomes no longer appropriate for any other reason` MEANS
        `a provision of an Act refers to an authority`
    AND (   `the authority is abolished`
         OR `the name or title of the authority is changed`
         OR `there is a change in the matters dealt with by the authority because of the effect of an Administrative Arrangements Order`
         OR `the reference to the authority becomes no longer appropriate for any other reason`)

-- (2) The power of the Governor-General to direct that the provision is to have effect, from a day specified in the order, as if
-- the reference were to another specified authority. (6) bars an order made only because an authority was abolished and, at once,
-- another of the same type and name was established; the Note to (6) keeps (1)(b)(iii) and (iv) open.
-- src:484 | (2) The Governor-General may make a substituted reference order directing that the provision is to have effect for all purposes, on and after a day specified in the order:
-- src:485 | (a) as if there were substituted, for the reference to the authority mentioned in subsection (1), a reference to another specified authority (or authorities); or
-- src:486 | (b) as if, in so far as the provision applies in a particular respect specified in the order, there were substituted, for the reference to the authority mentioned in subsection (1), a reference to another specified authority (or authorities).
-- src:494 | (6) A substituted reference order must not be made only because an authority is abolished, and, immediately after its abolition, another authority of the same type, with the same name, is established.
-- src:495 | Note: However, a substituted reference order may be made if either of the following happens in relation to the authority:
-- src:496 | (a) there is a change in the matters dealt with by the authority because of the effect of an Administrative Arrangements Order (see subparagraph (1)(b)(iii));
-- src:497 | (b) a reference to the authority becomes no longer appropriate for any other reason (see subparagraph (1)(b)(iv)).
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19B(2) and (6) (src:484-497)
GIVEN `a provision of an Act refers to an authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority is abolished` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name or title of the authority is changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a change in the matters dealt with by the authority because of the effect of an Administrative Arrangements Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference to the authority becomes no longer appropriate for any other reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another authority of the same type and with the same name was established immediately after the abolition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Governor-General may make a substituted reference order` `a provision of an Act refers to an authority` `the authority is abolished` `the name or title of the authority is changed` `there is a change in the matters dealt with by the authority because of the effect of an Administrative Arrangements Order` `the reference to the authority becomes no longer appropriate for any other reason` `another authority of the same type and with the same name was established immediately after the abolition` MEANS
        `a provision of an Act refers to an authority`
    AND (   (`the authority is abolished` AND (NOT `another authority of the same type and with the same name was established immediately after the abolition`))
         OR `the name or title of the authority is changed`
         OR `there is a change in the matters dealt with by the authority because of the effect of an Administrative Arrangements Order`
         OR `the reference to the authority becomes no longer appropriate for any other reason`)

-- src:489 | (3) The day specified in the order (as the day on and after which the order is to have effect) may be a day before the order is made.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19B(3) (src:489)
GIVEN `the day specified in the order` IS A DATE
      `the day the order is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day on and after which the order has effect` `the day specified in the order` `the day the order is made` MEANS
    `the day specified in the order`

-- (2) "on and after a day specified in the order": the order is in effect on a day that is not before the specified day, even if
-- the specified day is earlier than the day the order was made (subsection (3)).
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19B(2) and (3) (src:489)
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the day specified in the order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the order is in effect on` `the day in question` `the order specifies the day` `the day specified in the order` MEANS
    `the day in question` AT LEAST `the day specified in the order`

-- src:490 | (4) A substituted reference order has effect according to its terms.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19B(4) (src:490)
GIVEN `it is a substituted reference order made under section 19B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`has effect according to its terms` `it is a substituted reference order made under section 19B` MEANS
    IF `it is a substituted reference order made under section 19B` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:492 | (5) A substituted reference order is a legislative instrument.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19B(5) (src:492)
GIVEN `it is a substituted reference order made under section 19B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is a legislative instrument` `it is a substituted reference order made under section 19B` MEANS
    IF `it is a substituted reference order made under section 19B` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 19C: references to authorities in Commonwealth agreements`

DECLARE `Authority referred to in a Commonwealth agreement` IS ONE OF
    `a Minister`
    `a Department`
    `any other authority`

DECLARE `Authority the agreement is taken to refer to` IS ONE OF
    `the Minister, or any of the Ministers, administering the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter on the relevant day`
    `the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter on the relevant day`
    `an authority (including the relevant authority) exercising the powers, or performing the functions, of the relevant authority on the relevant day`
    `an authority (including the relevant authority) determined under subsection (4)`

-- src:508 | (1) This section applies if:
-- src:509 | (a) a provision of an agreement entered into by or on behalf of the Commonwealth refers to an authority (see subsection (6)) in relation to a particular matter (the relevant matter); and
-- src:510 | (b) any of the following happens after the agreement was entered into:
-- src:511 | (i) the authority is abolished;
-- src:512 | (ii) the name or title of the authority is changed;
-- src:513 | (iii) there is a change in the matters dealt with by the authority because of the effect of an Administrative Arrangements Order;
-- src:514 | (iv) the reference to the authority becomes no longer appropriate for any other reason.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19C(1) (src:508-514)
GIVEN `a provision of an agreement entered into by or on behalf of the Commonwealth refers to an authority in relation to a particular matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority is abolished after the agreement was entered into` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name or title of the authority is changed after the agreement was entered into` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a change in the matters dealt with by the authority because of the effect of an Administrative Arrangements Order after the agreement was entered into` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference to the authority becomes no longer appropriate for any other reason after the agreement was entered into` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 19C applies` `a provision of an agreement entered into by or on behalf of the Commonwealth refers to an authority in relation to a particular matter` `the authority is abolished after the agreement was entered into` `the name or title of the authority is changed after the agreement was entered into` `there is a change in the matters dealt with by the authority because of the effect of an Administrative Arrangements Order after the agreement was entered into` `the reference to the authority becomes no longer appropriate for any other reason after the agreement was entered into` MEANS
        `a provision of an agreement entered into by or on behalf of the Commonwealth refers to an authority in relation to a particular matter`
    AND (   `the authority is abolished after the agreement was entered into`
         OR `the name or title of the authority is changed after the agreement was entered into`
         OR `there is a change in the matters dealt with by the authority because of the effect of an Administrative Arrangements Order after the agreement was entered into`
         OR `the reference to the authority becomes no longer appropriate for any other reason after the agreement was entered into`)

-- src:516 | (2) The following table provides which authority the provision of the agreement is taken to refer to in relation to the relevant matter on a particular day (the relevant day) after the most recent event mentioned in paragraph (1)(b).
-- src:517 | References to authorities in Commonwealth agreements
-- src:518 | Item
-- src:519 | If the provision refers to …
-- src:520 | then the provision is taken to refer to …
-- src:521 | 1
-- src:522 | a Minister
-- src:523 | the Minister, or any of the Ministers, administering the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter on the relevant day.
-- src:524 | 2
-- src:525 | a Department
-- src:526 | the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter on the relevant day.
-- src:527 | 3
-- src:528 | any other authority (the relevant authority)
-- src:529 | an authority (including the relevant authority):
-- src:530 | (a) exercising the powers, or performing the functions, of the relevant authority on the relevant day; or
-- src:531 | (b) determined under subsection (4).
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19C(2) (src:516-531)
GIVEN referred IS A `Authority referred to in a Commonwealth agreement`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Authority the agreement is taken to refer to`
`the authorities an agreement is taken to refer to` referred MEANS
    CONSIDER referred
    WHEN `a Minister` THEN
        LIST `the Minister, or any of the Ministers, administering the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter on the relevant day`
    WHEN `a Department` THEN
        LIST `the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter on the relevant day`
    WHEN `any other authority` THEN
        LIST `an authority (including the relevant authority) exercising the powers, or performing the functions, of the relevant authority on the relevant day`,
             `an authority (including the relevant authority) determined under subsection (4)`

-- src:532 | (3) The following instruments, as in force on the relevant day, or any earlier day, may be used to work out which authority is taken to be referred to under subsection (2):
-- src:533 | (a) an Administrative Arrangements Order;
-- src:534 | (b) a substituted reference order under section 19B.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19C(3) (src:532-534)
GIVEN instrument IS A `Instrument that may be used to work out the reference`
      `it is in force on the relevant day or was in force on an earlier day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`may be used to work out which authority is taken to be referred to` instrument `it is in force on the relevant day or was in force on an earlier day` MEANS
    CONSIDER instrument
    WHEN `any other instrument` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE IF `it is in force on the relevant day or was in force on an earlier day` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:536 | (4) The Minister administering the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter may, by notifiable instrument, make a determination for the purposes of item 3 of the table in subsection (2).
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19C(4) (src:536)
GIVEN `it is made by the Minister administering the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made by notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a determination for the purposes of item 3` `it is made by the Minister administering the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter` `it is made by notifiable instrument` MEANS
    `it is made by the Minister administering the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter` AND `it is made by notifiable instrument`

-- src:539 | (5) To avoid doubt, if, because of this section, a provision of an agreement entered into by or on behalf of the Commonwealth is taken to require anything to be done by or in relation to any one of 2 or more Ministers, the provision is not taken to require it to be done in any particular case by or in relation to more than one of those Ministers.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19C(5) (src:539)
GIVEN `the number of Ministers by or in relation to any one of whom the provision of the agreement is taken to require a thing to be done` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the most Ministers by or in relation to whom the agreement requires the thing to be done in a particular case` `the number of Ministers by or in relation to any one of whom the provision of the agreement is taken to require a thing to be done` MEANS
    IF `the number of Ministers by or in relation to any one of whom the provision of the agreement is taken to require a thing to be done` AT LEAST 2 THEN JUST 1 ELSE NOTHING

-- src:541 | (6) In this section:
-- src:542 | authority means any of the following:
-- src:543 | (a) a Minister;
-- src:544 | (b) a Department of State of the Commonwealth;
-- src:545 | (c) any other Agency within the meaning of the Public Service Act 1999;
-- src:546 | (d) an office (including an APS employee’s office and any other appointment or position), or the holder of an office.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19C(6) (src:541-546)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of authority`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is an authority within section 19C` kind MEANS
    NOT (kind EQUALS `something else`)

§§ `Section 19D: saving the validity of acts done by authorities`

DECLARE `Ground in section 19D(1)` IS ONE OF
    `the power, function or duty is conferred or imposed on another authority`
    `the power, function or duty is conferred or imposed on the same authority under another name or title`
    `the power, function or duty is no longer conferred or imposed on any authority`
    `some other ground`

DECLARE `Source of the power, function or duty` IS ONE OF
    `an Act or legislative instrument`
    `an agreement entered into by or on behalf of the Commonwealth`
    `any other authorisation under a law of the Commonwealth`
    `some other source`

-- src:556 | (3) For the purposes of this section, a machinery of government change occurs if any of the following applies in relation to an authority:
-- src:557 | (a) the authority is abolished;
-- src:558 | (b) the name or title of the authority is changed;
-- src:559 | (c) there is a change in the matters dealt with by the authority because of the effect of an Administrative Arrangements Order;
-- src:560 | (d) the authority no longer exercises or performs the power, function or duty for any other reason.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19D(3) (src:556-560)
GIVEN `the authority is abolished` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name or title of the authority is changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a change in the matters dealt with by the authority because of the effect of an Administrative Arrangements Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority no longer exercises or performs the power, function or duty for any other reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a machinery of government change occurs` `the authority is abolished` `the name or title of the authority is changed` `there is a change in the matters dealt with by the authority because of the effect of an Administrative Arrangements Order` `the authority no longer exercises or performs the power, function or duty for any other reason` MEANS
        `the authority is abolished`
     OR `the name or title of the authority is changed`
     OR `there is a change in the matters dealt with by the authority because of the effect of an Administrative Arrangements Order`
     OR `the authority no longer exercises or performs the power, function or duty for any other reason`

-- (1) The purported exercise is "not invalid merely because" of the change, on the grounds (a), (b) or (c); (2) only if the authority
-- acted on a reasonable, but mistaken, belief about the occurrence, timing or nature of the change; (4) for a power under an Act
-- or legislative instrument, a Commonwealth agreement, or another authorisation under a law of the Commonwealth. The section
-- saves; it does not say that an act outside it IS invalid, so the answer outside the section is NOTHING. Subsection (1) is "subject
-- to section 19E", which also saves an act done by a Minister under another Minister's power; the two do not conflict and
-- no case in this text takes protection away.
-- src:550 | (1) Subject to section 19E, the purported exercise or performance of a power, function or duty by or on behalf of an authority (see subsection (5)) is not invalid merely because, following a machinery of government change, the power, function or duty:
-- src:551 | (a) is conferred or imposed on another authority; or
-- src:552 | (b) is conferred or imposed on the same authority under another name or title; or
-- src:553 | (c) is no longer conferred or imposed on any authority.
-- src:554 | (2) Subsection (1) only applies if the authority acted on the basis of a reasonable, but mistaken, belief about the occurrence, timing or nature of the machinery of government change.
-- src:562 | (4) This section applies in relation to a power, function or duty purportedly exercised or performed by or on behalf of an authority, whether before or after the machinery of government change, under any of the following:
-- src:563 | (a) an Act or legislative instrument;
-- src:564 | (b) an agreement entered into by or on behalf of the Commonwealth;
-- src:565 | (c) any other authorisation under a law of the Commonwealth.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19D(1), (2) and (4) (src:550-565)
GIVEN ground IS A `Ground in section 19D(1)`
      `a machinery of government change occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority acted on the basis of a reasonable, but mistaken, belief about the occurrence, timing or nature of the machinery of government change` IS A BOOLEAN
      source IS A `Source of the power, function or duty`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the purported exercise is not invalid merely because of the change` ground `a machinery of government change occurred` `the authority acted on the basis of a reasonable, but mistaken, belief about the occurrence, timing or nature of the machinery of government change` source MEANS
    IF     (NOT (ground EQUALS `some other ground`))
       AND `a machinery of government change occurred`
       AND `the authority acted on the basis of a reasonable, but mistaken, belief about the occurrence, timing or nature of the machinery of government change`
       AND (NOT (source EQUALS `some other source`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:567 | (5) In this section:
-- src:568 | authority means any of the following persons or bodies:
-- src:569 | (a) a Minister;
-- src:570 | (b) a Department of State of the Commonwealth;
-- src:571 | (c) any other Agency within the meaning of the Public Service Act 1999;
-- src:572 | (d) an office (including an APS employee’s office and any other appointment or position), or the holder of an office.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19D(5) (src:567-572)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of authority`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is an authority within section 19D` kind MEANS
    NOT (kind EQUALS `something else`)

§§ `Section 19E: validity of acts done by Ministers`

-- src:574 | 19E Validity of acts done by Ministers
-- src:575 | If a Minister purports to exercise a power or perform a function or duty that is conferred or imposed on another Minister by an Act, the exercise of that power or the performance of that function or duty is not invalid merely because the power, function or duty is conferred or imposed on the other Minister.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 19E (src:574-575)
GIVEN `a Minister purports to exercise a power or perform a function or duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is conferred or imposed on another Minister by an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the exercise is not invalid merely because the power is conferred on the other Minister` `a Minister purports to exercise a power or perform a function or duty` `it is conferred or imposed on another Minister by an Act` MEANS
    IF `a Minister purports to exercise a power or perform a function or duty` AND `it is conferred or imposed on another Minister by an Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
